nely competitive.", "watch": "A decisive national Democratic wave, or the nomination of an unusually strong or flawed candidate on either side, could move the margin, though an outright Democratic win remains a long shot.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "North Dakota is among the most Republican-leaning states in the country, and a presidential race there starts with a steep structural advantage for the Republican nominee. The state has backed Republican presidential candidates by wide margins in recent cycles, and its partisan lean of roughly eighteen points Republican sets the starting point for this open-seat contest.\n\nNo state-level polls, expert ratings, or campaign finance figures are available yet, and both major parties' nominees remain undetermined. That leaves fundamentals to carry the forecast: a strong Republican lean, no incumbent on the ballot, and no local evidence of a competitive environment. National political conditions could move the margin by a few points in either direction, but closing an eighteen-point gap would require a shift well beyond anything recent cycles have produced in the state. The race is rated Safe Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0273, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0549, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0572, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0505, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0556, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0598, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin